{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"2fae4c07-96f1-415a-9447-ce775baf972b","status":"SUCCESS","response":"HereHere is the analysis of why your launchd task was silently failing and the exact fixes applied.\n\n- **Root causes** (taken from the colleague’s note):\n  1. `zsh`’s read‑only variable `status` was overwritten, causing the script to abort before any error notification.\n  2. The `claude` headless agent expected its prompt on **stdin**, but the script passed it as an argument, leading to an immediate “Input must be provided …” failure.\n\n- **What was fixed**:\n  - Replaced `status=$?` with a safe variable `rc=$?`.\n  - Updated the failure check to use `$rc`.\n  - Fed the prompt to `claude` through a pipe: `print -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p - …`.\n  - Adjusted the notification messages to reference `$rc`.\n\n- **Full updated script** (`nightly-review.zsh`):\n\n```zsh\n#!/bin/zsh\n# Nightly review of yesterday's commits, summary to Telegram.\nset -u\n\nREPO=\"$HOME/projects/shop\"\nOUT=\"$HOME/Library/Logs/nightly-review-$(date +%F).md\"\nNOTIFY=\"$HOME/bin/notify.sh\"\n\nSINCE=$(date -v-1d +%F)\nPROMPT=\"Review the commits in this repository since $SINCE.\nFor each commit: one line on what it changes and whether anything looks risky\n(migrations, auth, payments, deleted tests).\nEnd with a three-line summary I can read on my phone.\nDo not modify any file.\"\n\ncd \"$REPO\" || { \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review: repo missing\"; exit 1; }\n\n# Feed the prompt via stdin so claude works under launchd\nprint -r -- \"$PROMPT\" | claude -p - --output-format text \u003e \"$OUT\"\nrc=$?\n\nif [ $rc -ne 0 ]; then\n  \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $rc), see $OUT\"\n  exit $rc\nfi\n\n\"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review done: $(head -c 300 \"$OUT\")\"\n```\n\n- **Additional recommendations** (also from the note):\n  - Add `USER` to `EnvironmentVariables` in the plist if `claude` needs Keychain access.\n  - Log execution time (e.g., with `time`) to catch quick‑exit failures.\n  - Verify the real output file (`$OUT`) and its timestamp rather than solely relying on exit codes.\n\nAll findings and applied changes are documented in **[ANSWER.md](file:///Users/valentinakoniukhova/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/2fae4c07-96f1-415a-9447-ce775baf972b/ANSWER.md)**.\n","duration_seconds":90.14875,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":18716,"output_tokens":7123,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":219776,"total_tokens":25839}}}
